bug found (why v1 failed): two independent errors in the ticks-5-7 generalization:
  (a) Re[w^{ic}] = cos(c ln w) is only valid for REAL c. For complex z the correct
      identity is cos(theta) = (e^{i theta}+e^{-i theta})/2, giving TWO gamma terms:
      J(a,z,n) = (1/8)*[P^{-sp} Gamma(sp,P) + P^{-sm} Gamma(sm,P)], sp=(a+iz)/4, sm=(a-iz)/4
      (the one-term Re form is the z-real special case; it passed the real-axis test).
  (b) the first correction attempt double-counted the P^{-a/4} factor (it appears once,
      from e^{au} = (v/X)^{a/4} in the substitution v = X e^{4u}), giving -0.0003064877
      +0.0002172399i; the corrected formula reproduces the direct quadrature.
bonus finding (oracle trap): the 64-digit value hardcoded in
  dbn_upper_bound/tests/python/test_ht.py is Ht_AFE_ABC(35+10j, 0) with N = int(tau) = 1
  (tau = sqrt(Im(s)/2pi) = 1.669, s = (1+iz)/2 = -4.5+17.5i) — an approximate functional
  equation output, NOT the exact H_0. Exact value (term-by-term direct u-quadrature,
  mpmath 70 digits, n=1..5, converges by n=3):
  H_0(35+10j) = 0.00032163883436158191156597555258989525738957951903864280036118553936386
              + 0.00007319227113411741599835095251496972054311906234081401086774973830934 i
  AFE N=1 differs by ~2.5%. Do not use test_ht.py values as exact oracles.
