bugs found and fixed (root-caused, all verified in scratch before touching the repo):
  1) mp.findroot (single start, no df) returns DUPLICATE roots for Legendre P_n
     (n=32: 3 dups; sum of mapped weights 1.074 vs 1 on [0,1]) and fails to converge
     at n=64. Replaced by Newton with polynomial-derivative (Horner) eval on
     recurrence coefficients: starts 1-1.8657/n^2 (k=1), its negative (k=n),
     else cos(pi*(k-0.25)/(n+0.5)); stop |f|<1e-115 or |step|<1e-118; asserts
     residual<1e-110, distinct, in (-1,1). Verified: n=16/32/64 all roots,
     maxresid ~1e-110..1e-116, no dups, moments ~1e-122.
  2) the "tick 14 fix" (weight w = 2(1-x^2)^2/(n^2 P_{n-1}^2)) was a MISDIAGNOSIS:
     the correct identity is the SINGLE-factor w = 2(1-x^2)/(n^2 P_{n-1}^2)
     (n=2 check: w=1,w=1 exact; P_n' identity: w = 2/((1-x^2)[nP_{n-1}/(1-x^2)]^2)).
     The moment failures were from the findroot dups, not the weights.
  3) apparent 1e-17 moment deviations in scratch debugging were a Python-float
     2/(k+1) target (2/3 as float = 0.66666666666666661, off by 3.7e-17); the repo
     moment test uses exact acb targets — no bug there.
  4) acb ball-vs-ball comparisons crash (gp.real < 0): added _re_upper/_re_lower
     float-bound helpers for the tail asserts.
  5) digits_agree: 10**(-exp) is a float for negative exponents (Decimal*float crash
     on |value|>1, i.e. t=100); rewrote mantissa extraction via format(x,'.59E').
  6) checker's float(qt.rad()) overflows float64 for |value|~1e500 (t=1000) -> inf;
     rel radius now computed in mpmath from the ball strings.
